# 2. FIRST ASSIGNMENT: AUDIT AND STABILIZE THE EXISTING SDK

Before expanding the platform:

- Inspect every Maven module, class, service, repository, controller, migration, test and dependency.
- Map all existing domain capabilities to their owning modules.
- Identify duplicated services and competing sources of truth.
- Identify missing persistence, security, validation and audit functionality.
- Fix the existing Maven dependency-resolution failure.
- Execute the full Maven build and existing test suites.
- Establish database migration verification.
- Address critical tenant-isolation defects.
- Remove memory-only storage from clinical or regulated business operations.
- Correct false or unsupported documentation claims.
- Maintain an implementation and evidence register.

Preserve functional code rather than needlessly rewriting it.

For each reusable module, record:

- Module ID and artifact coordinates
- Domain ownership
- Implemented capabilities
- Public interfaces and APIs
- Required dependencies
- Optional integrations
- Configurable features
- Database migrations
- Security requirements
- Test coverage
- Known limitations
- Release-readiness status

Do not claim the existing SDK is production-ready merely because its class structure is complete.

