Do not duplicate foundational capabilities across industry packs.

Use existing HealthCore modules where suitable and introduce missing shared foundations where necessary.

Establish clear contracts for:

1. Authentication and authorization
2. Tenant/organization/facility context
3. Audit events and electronic signatures
4. Workflow orchestration
5. Configurable forms and validation
6. Document rendering and storage
7. Notifications
8. Scheduling and calendar infrastructure
9. Event publishing and subscriptions
10. Transactional outbox/inbox
11. Inventory primitives and traceability
12. Financial ledger integration
13. Terminology and reference data
14. Device and instrument integration
15. Data import/export
16. Reporting and analytics
17. Offline sync
18. API security and integration governance
19. Regulatory configuration and retention policies
20. Provenance and immutable record history

Shared infrastructure must remain domain-neutral.

Do not force unrelated domains to share mutable JPA entities simply because their business objects have similar names. Use explicit mapping contracts and domain adapters.

For example, a clinical specimen, a research biospecimen and a pharmaceutical QC sample may share barcode infrastructure but must retain distinct domain semantics.

