# 16. ULTIMATE SUCCESS CRITERIA

A developer must be able to:

- Build standalone pharmacy software without installing an HIS.
- Build diagnostic laboratory software without installing pharmacy or inpatient modules.
- Build radiology software without deploying a complete LIS.
- Build pharmaceutical manufacturing software without needing patient records or EMR services.
- Build a life-science LIMS or ELN without hospital dependencies.
- Build an EMR using a small selection of clinical modules.
- Build an EHR using longitudinal care and interoperability modules.
- Build a hospital HIS by composing relevant modules.
- Build an HIE without deploying hospital business workflows.
- Integrate selected HealthCore capabilities into an existing independent application through stable Java APIs or documented REST interfaces.

Every example must perform real persisted operations, pass its required tests and have working integration documentation.

**The final objective is an industry-grade reusable SDK that reduces development effort, preserves developer independence, and supplies trustworthy, well-tested healthcare and life-science building blocks.**

Begin by auditing the current repository against this directive, stabilizing existing functionality and implementing the missing reusable capabilities in dependency order. Do not confuse the framework with an end-user application. Do not claim success without verification evidence.
